meta {
  name: 03 - Rejects an invalid signature
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  content-type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {"type":1}
}

script:pre-request {
  // Runs after the collection script, so this replaces whatever it signed.
  req.setHeader('x-signature-ed25519', 'ff'.repeat(64));
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 401
}

docs {
  Discord's own probe. It sends deliberately invalid signatures to a new
  endpoint and refuses to register a URL that accepts them, so a 401 here is a
  requirement rather than a nicety.
  
  This is the one request worth running before anything else is configured: it
  needs no key, and it proves the endpoint is reachable and guarded.
}
